  "summary_en": "Bilingual consolidated Manitoba Workplace Safety and Health Regulation (M.R. 217/2006), current to October 2026. It sets general workplace safety duties across 44 parts, including a dedicated Part 16 on machines, tools and robots (ss. 16.29-16.33), powered mobile equipment and lift trucks. It is general occupational safety law with no AI content.",
  "key_provisions_or_claims": [
   "Employers must eliminate or control risks via design, engineering controls, safe work procedures, then PPE",
   "Part 16 regulates machines, tools and robots (robot, robot system and restricted work envelope defined)",
   "Serious incidents must be reported immediately, preserved and investigated",
   "Safety committees, worker representatives and exemption orders by the director",
   "Incorporates CSA/ANSI/ISO standards by reference"
  ],
